    "terminal_reason": "completed",
    "result_text": "I've implemented `summarize_ticket` in `app/summary.py`:\n\n```python\ndef summarize_ticket(chat: BaseChatModel, ticket: Ticket) -> str:\n    \"\"\"A one-sentence summary of `ticket`; generation stops at the first blank line.\"\"\"\n    messages = [SystemMessage(SUMMARY_PROMPT), HumanMessage(ticket_text(ticket))]\n    reply = chat.invoke(messages, stop=[\"\\n\\n\"])\n    # `.text` also handles providers that return a list of content blocks instead of a str.\n    return str(reply.text).strip()\n```\n\nIt makes one `invoke` call with the system and user messages, passes the stop sequence through the standard `stop=` argument, and trims whitespace from the reply.\n\nI used `reply.text` instead of `str(reply.content)` on purpose. Some chat models, such as Anthropic's, return a list of content blocks, and `str()` on that list would produce something like `\"[{'type': 'text', ...}]\"` instead of the reply text. `.text` gets the text either way.\n\n**Checks:**\n- `pytest -q` passes (2 tests), but no existing test covers `summarize_ticket`.\n- I also ran it against LangChain's fake chat model with a spy added. That confirmed exactly one call with `[SystemMessage, HumanMessage]` and `stop=['\\n\\n']`. Both a plain-string reply and a content-block reply came back as trimmed strings: `'Login fails for Acme.'` and `'Blocks work.'`.\n\n**Cleanup needed:** I couldn't delete the temporary script `_check_summary.py` from the project root because removing files needs your approval. Please delete it, or turn it into a proper test under `tests/` if you'd like one."
